{"id": "28", "question": "The force exerted on an object and distance traveled have what kind of relationship?", "step_idx": 0, "options": ["A): reverse", "B): inverse", "C): equal", "D): direct"], "correct": "D", "initial_cot": "The force exerted on an object is related to the distance traveled in a way that is opposite to the relationship between the force and the distance traveled in a simple harmonic motion. In simple harmonic motion, the force is proportional to the distance traveled. In contrast, the force exerted on an object is inversely proportional to the distance traveled. This is because the force required to move an object is greater when the object is at rest and decreases as the object moves. Therefore, the correct answer is (B): inverse.\nThe best answer is B.<|eot_id|>", "initial_cot_probs": [0.0, 1.0, 0.0, 0.0], "initial_probs": [0.024291452020406723, 0.7099003195762634, 0.031190842390060425, 0.23047088086605072], "prediction": 1, "cot_prediction": 1, "cot_step": "The force exerted on an object is related to the distance traveled in a way that is opposite to the relationship between the force and the distance traveled in a simple harmonic motion.", "segmented_cot": ["The force exerted on an object is related to the distance traveled in a way that is opposite to the relationship between the force and the distance traveled in a simple harmonic motion.", "In simple harmonic motion, the force is proportional to the distance traveled.", "In contrast, the force exerted on an object is inversely proportional to the distance traveled.", "This is because the force required to move an object is greater when the object is at rest and decreases as the object moves.", "Therefore, the correct answer is (B): inverse.", "The best answer is B.<|eot_id|>"], "unlearning_results": {"0": {"completion": "B): inverse. The force exerted on an", "probs": [0.024291452020406723, 0.7099003195762634, 0.031190842390060425, 0.23047088086605072], "prediction": 1, "target_cot_step